SUMMARY:ABCD Reads "Whistler" by Ann Patchett
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads "**[Whistler](https:
 //tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4751790)**" by Ann Patchett\n\n[[RE
 SULTS](https://opavote.com/results/5448125428006912) of the poll for this 
 event]\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n"When Daphne Fuller and her husband Jo
 nathan visit the Metropolitan Museum of Art\, they notice an older\, white
 -haired gentleman following them. The man turns out to be Eddie Triplett\,
  her former stepfather\, who had been married to her mother for a little m
 ore than year when Daphne was nine. [...]\nWhistler is a story about two a
 dults looking back over the choices they made\, and the choices that were 
 made for them. It’s a story about bravery\, memory\, the often small yet
  consequential moments that define our lives\, and the endless stream of l
 oss that in time comes for us all. Beautiful in its simplicity\, it is ult
 imately about how love endures\, and how the feeling of being known by one
  other person\, even for a short period of time\, can change everything." 
 (from [Goodreads](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/242693052-whistler))
 \n\n"Now fifty-three\, Daphne hasn’t seen Eddie for many years\, not sin
 ce the fateful event that changed the direction of both their lives. Meeti
 ng again\, time falls away\; while their relationship was brief\, it had a
  profound impact on them both\, and now that they are reunited\, they have
  no intention of ever being separated again." (from [BookMarks.reviews](ht
 tps://bookmarks.reviews/reviews/whistler/))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE EVENT ::**\n
 You are welcome to arrive 30 minutes before the event and stay 30 minutes 
 or longer afterward to connect with other attendees outside the book talk.
 \n\nPlease ensure you have read the book before attending (though finishin
 g any book is not a barrier to participating\, as long as you don't mind s
 poilers).\n\nFirst-time attendees can join for free. If the event is full\
 , we maintain an unofficial waitlist. Please send [Michael](https://www.me
 etup.com/members/55295192/) a direct message for more information\, in eit
 her case.\n\nWe request a $3 contribution from regular attendees to help c
 over our monthly meetup costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::**\nAt the en
 d of each event\, we will ask for nominees for our next book. If you have 
 a good one in mind\, please ensure it is between 200-400 pages long\, avai
 lable from the Toronto Public Library\, and counts as contemporary literar
 y fiction (though these are not hard and fast rules). When enough nominees
  are collected\, Michael will send the members a direct message with a lin
 k where you can vote.
